cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research artifact, please cite the public preprint using the
  preferred citation below.
title: >-
  When Aggregate Accuracy Is Not Enough: Decision Impact, Validation
  Governance, and a Causal Evaluation Blueprint for Financial Complaint Triage
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Ancheta
    given-names: Charles Jr
version: 1.0.2
date-released: 2026-07-29
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21670879
repository-code: https://github.com/cj-ancheta/Complaint-Triage
url: https://github.com/cj-ancheta/Complaint-Triage/releases/tag/paper-v1.0.2
abstract: >-
  This validation-only study compares TF-IDF logistic regression and compact
  MiniLM for imbalanced financial complaint routing, evaluates calibration and
  class-aware abstention, documents a negative manual-review-only release
  decision, and specifies a prospective randomized causal evaluation of
  human-AI decision support.
keywords:
  - consumer complaints
  - text classification
  - selective classification
  - model governance
  - causal inference
  - human-AI decision support
